1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,210
Sometimes, the thing that stops us from changing our life…

2
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:09,050
is our expectation that life will change on its own.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,040
Hello, and welcome to Cozy French Radio.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:12,920
It's Lia.

5
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,330
I'm really happy to be with you again today.

6
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:16,720
How are you?

7
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,130
Not just how you are when someone asks you

8
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:21,360
that question and you answer quickly:

9
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,560
"I'm fine, thanks."

10
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,540
No…

11
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:26,080
how are you, really?

12
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,880
Do you feel good in your life

13
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,750
right now?

14
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,400
Are you a little tired?

15
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,810
Or do you have that strange feeling that

16
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,240
something needs to change,

17
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,560
without knowing exactly what?

18
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,360
This morning, before starting this recording,

19
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:42,070
I stayed a few minutes by my window,

20
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:43,440
with a cup of hot coffee.

21
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,570
I was watching people go by in the street.

22
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:47,060
Some were walking fast.

23
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,980
Others were taking their time.

24
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,680
And a thought came to me.

25
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:53,090
We all move forward through our days.

26
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:56,220
But do we always move in the direction

27
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,210
that we want?

28
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,920
It's a simple question.

29
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:02,720
And yet, it can change the way we look at our life.

30
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,400
Today, we're going to talk about this idea:

31
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,920
Nothing changes if nothing changes.

32
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,210
In French, we can say:

33
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:13,880
"Rien ne change si rien ne change."

34
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,730
It's a very simple sentence.

35
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:17,160
Almost too simple.

36
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:20,480
But sometimes, the most important truths don't

37
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,840
need many words.

38
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,220
And while you listen,

39
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:26,260
you can also practise your French calmly.

40
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:28,920
You don't need to understand every expression.

41
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,840
Just let the words come,

42
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,160
like in a conversation with a friend.

43
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,720
Now imagine a scene.

44
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,390
It's Sunday evening.

45
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:39,600
Someone is sitting on their sofa.

46
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:43,440
They look at their phone and think about the week ahead.

47
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,110
They tell themselves: "On Monday,

48
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:47,640
I'm going to start a new life."

49
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,060
They want to eat better,

50
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,480
go to bed earlier, learn a language,

51
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:54,350
do some sport, take time for themselves.

52
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,970
They have lots of plans.

53
00:01:55,970 --> 00:01:57,480
And they mean it.

54
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,150
But Monday comes.

55
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:00,640
The alarm rings.

56
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,880
They're tired.

57
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,640
They check their messages.

58
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,240
They leave for work.

59
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,760
In the evening, they come home and fall back into their habits.

60
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,180
Then Sunday comes.

61
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:13,000
And they make themselves the same promise again.

62
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,320
Maybe you know this situation.

63
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:18,120
We've all waited for a special Monday,

64
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,470
a new month, a new year.

65
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:24,280
As if a date could automatically give us new energy.

66
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:28,160
But the calendar can change without our habits changing.

67
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:31,680
That's where the first truth of our conversation lies.

68
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:35,000
A new date doesn't create a new direction.

69
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,020
It's a choice, even a small one,

70
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:39,280
that can start to do that.

71
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:42,000
You don't need to transform your life today.

72
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,360
You can simply stop waiting for the perfect moment.

73
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,520
Because sometimes, the first change isn't in

74
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,590
what you do.

75
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,650
It's in this little sentence that you

76
00:02:51,650 --> 00:02:55,420
tell yourself inside: "I can start with what I have,

77
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:56,760
right where I am."

78
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:59,060
And that thought, on its own,

79
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,840
already opens a door.

80
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,400
There's a strange thing in our lives.

81
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:06,160
We can be unhappy in a situation…

82
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,640
and yet not want to leave it.

83
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:09,560
Why?

84
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,220
Because a familiar situation can seem more reassuring to us

85
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,760
than an unknown one.

86
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,190
Even when it no longer makes us happy.

87
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,920
Imagine someone who always takes the same route

88
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,360
to get home.

89
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:24,040
Every day, they walk down the same streets.

90
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,040
They pass the same shops.

91
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,240
They wait at the same red light.

92
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,520
The journey is long.

93
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:32,160
There's a lot of noise and traffic.

94
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:35,120
One day, someone tells them about another route.

95
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,520
A calmer route,

96
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,480
nicer, maybe even shorter.

97
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,840
But they hesitate.

98
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,360
"What if I get lost?

99
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,830
What if this route isn't really better?"

100
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:48,280
So, the next day, they take their old route again.

101
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,680
Not because they like it.

102
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,720
Simply because they know it.

103
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:54,520
And sometimes we do the same thing with our life.

104
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:57,000
We keep habits that wear us out.

105
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,400
We stay in some relationships that are no longer good for us.

106
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,140
We stay in situations that no longer match

107
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:03,960
our needs.

108
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,960
Not because we're happy.

109
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:07,790
But because we're afraid of what

110
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:10,040
might happen if we changed.

111
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,710
Do you see the paradox?

112
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:17,080
Sometimes, we prefer a known discomfort to an unknown possibility.

113
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:18,160
It's human.

114
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,920
Our mind likes to recognise things.

115
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,160
It likes to know what's going to happen.

116
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,280
When a situation is familiar,

117
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:28,640
even a difficult one, we know how to react.

118
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,600
But when something changes,

119
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,240
we have to learn all over again.

120
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,920
And learning takes energy.

121
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:37,960
Maybe you know this feeling with French.

122
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,840
You understand simple sentences.

123
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,670
You can listen to a podcast.

124
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,280
You recognise lots of words.

125
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,280
But when you get the chance to speak,

126
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,640
you sometimes prefer to stay silent.

127
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,600
Why?

128
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,250
Because in silence,

129
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:51,640
you don't make mistakes.

130
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,840
You feel protected.

131
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:56,120
But if you never speak,

132
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,680
you can't discover all the things that

133
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,960
you're already able to say.

134
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,840
The same thing happens in many areas.

135
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:09,030
We want to make progress, but we also want to avoid discomfort.

136
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,960
And the two wishes can come into conflict.

137
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,800
There's something important to understand here.

138
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:17,360
Comfort isn't bad.

139
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,680
We all need safety,

140
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,440
rest and reassuring habits.

141
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:25,080
A quiet place after a hard day,

142
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,560
a morning routine,

143
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:28,480
someone you trust…

144
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,360
All of that is precious.

145
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:33,720
The problem starts when comfort becomes a reason

146
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,830
to stop listening to what we truly want.

147
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,840
So, how can you tell the difference?

148
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,680
Ask yourself a question.

149
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,120
"Is this habit good for me…

150
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:47,440
or does it just keep me from being afraid?"

151
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:49,800
The answer may be surprising.

152
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,720
You can love your routine while needing something new.

153
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:58,400
You can appreciate your current situation while wanting something else.

154
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,970
You don't need to hate your life

155
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:02,390
to want to change it.

156
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:06,160
And above all, changing doesn't always mean leaving,

157
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,600
quitting or starting from scratch.

158
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:12,700
Sometimes, it simply means opening a window in a

159
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,600
room you've known for a long time.

160
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,080
The air can come in.

161
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,560
The light too.

162
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,400
And you may discover that you still have plenty

163
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,000
of room to grow.

164
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,240
There's a sentence we often tell ourselves.

165
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,840
"I'm not ready."

166
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,800
I'm not ready to start.

167
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:30,430
I'm not ready to speak French with someone.

168
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,840
I'm not ready to look for another job.

169
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:35,920
I'm not ready to make this decision.

170
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:39,240
But sometimes, behind "I'm not ready",

171
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,400
there's another sentence.

172
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,880
"I'm scared."

173
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,560
And that's not exactly the same thing.

174
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:48,720
Imagine a woman sitting at her computer.

175
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,560
She's looking at a job offer.

176
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,520
The position really interests her.

177
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:53,960
She has experience,

178
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:56,790
she knows the field and she'd love to work

179
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:58,310
for this company.

180
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,460
But she doesn't click the button to

181
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,040
send her application.

182
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:05,920
She thinks: "There are surely people better than me."

183
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:08,400
"My French maybe isn't good enough."

184
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,580
"And what if I get an interview and I

185
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,000
don't know how to answer?"

186
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,200
So she closes the page.

187
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,510
A few days later,

188
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,440
she finds the same ad again.

189
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,040
She hesitates again.

190
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,720
And in the end, the offer disappears.

191
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,770
What stopped her

192
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:25,860
wasn't necessarily a lack of ability.

193
00:07:25,910 --> 00:07:28,760
It was the fear of not being good enough.

194
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:32,040
Maybe you've already felt something similar.

195
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:34,840
This fear can take several forms.

196
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:36,840
The fear of making a mistake.

197
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,000
The fear of what others think.

198
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,560
The fear of losing what we have.

199
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,560
Or even the fear of succeeding,

200
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:47,800
because success can also bring new responsibilities.

201
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:52,060
And sometimes, we imagine so many possible problems that

202
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,750
we forget one essential question:

203
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,120
"What if things went well?"

204
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:00,080
We often think about what we could lose.

205
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:03,640
But we think less about what we could discover.

206
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:07,880
Of course, not every decision has to be made quickly.

207
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,000
Some situations need time,

208
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,800
thought and caution.

209
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:16,800
But there's a difference between taking time to think…

210
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:20,240
and simply waiting for the fear to go away.

211
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:23,350
Because fear doesn't always disappear before we act.

212
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:27,600
Sometimes, it gets smaller after our first step.

213
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,840
Think of someone learning to swim.

214
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,440
At first, the water can scare them.

215
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:35,280
This person can read books about swimming.

216
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,040
They can watch videos.

217
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:39,200
They can understand the movements.

218
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:42,200
But one day, with the right support,

219
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:46,240
they have to get in the water to really start learning.

220
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,200
They don't need to swim the whole length of the pool.

221
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,430
They can start near the edge.

222
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:54,240
And maybe that's exactly what we need

223
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,560
at other moments in our life.

224
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,640
Not huge courage.

225
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:03,080
Just enough courage to make a small move.

226
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:06,160
Here's an idea I'd like you to keep with you.

227
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:09,760
Courage isn't always the absence of fear.

228
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:13,020
Sometimes it's the decision not to let

229
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:15,600
fear choose for us.

230
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:18,120
You can be afraid and try.

231
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,790
You can doubt and keep going.

232
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,250
You can not know what comes next and take

233
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,360
a sensible first step.

234
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,080
And what if you get it wrong?

235
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:29,320
Then you'll learn something.

236
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:32,200
A mistake doesn't mean everything is over.

237
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:35,640
It can simply show you what works and

238
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,480
what doesn't.

239
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:40,880
Over time, we discover something surprising.

240
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:44,600
We don't always need confidence to start.

241
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:49,110
Sometimes, it's by starting that confidence appears.

242
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,040
When we think about change,

243
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:55,120
we often imagine something big.

244
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,790
A new house.

245
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:58,480
A new job.

246
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:00,880
A physical transformation.

247
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:04,960
A decision that changes our whole life.

248
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:07,690
But the most important changes aren't

249
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:09,760
always the most visible ones.

250
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:15,710
Sometimes, they're so small that nobody notices them.

251
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:19,040
Imagine someone who wants to learn French.

252
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:21,880
They set themselves a very ambitious goal.

253
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,260
"Starting tomorrow,

254
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:26,240
I'm going to study two hours every evening."

255
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,480
On the first day, they're motivated.

256
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,000
They get their notebooks ready.

257
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,960
They open several apps.

258
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,520
They watch videos.

259
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,600
They work for two hours.

260
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,080
On the second day, they do it again.

261
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,870
But on the third day,

262
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:42,360
they get home late.

263
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,870
They're tired.

264
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:46,240
They decide not to study.

265
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:48,960
The next day, they feel guilty.

266
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,840
Then they give up their plan.

267
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,510
A few weeks later,

268
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:56,000
they start again with a new goal,

269
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,920
just as hard as the first one.

270
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:02,000
Now, imagine another approach.

271
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,960
This person simply decides to listen to ten minutes of French every day.

272
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,240
Ten minutes.

273
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:10,590
While they make breakfast.

274
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,190
Or during a walk.

275
00:11:12,190 --> 00:11:14,000
They don't understand everything.

276
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,960
But they listen.

277
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:18,360
The next day, they do it again.

278
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:20,560
And the day after that too.

279
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:24,840
After a few weeks, some expressions become familiar.

280
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,800
They recognise sentences they didn't understand before.

281
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:30,840
They start to hear the words more clearly.

282
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:33,800
Nothing spectacular happened in a single day.

283
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:37,550
But something changed over time.

284
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,790
And here's a truth that can help us in

285
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:41,040
many areas.

286
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:44,820
A small change we can repeat is often

287
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:48,920
more useful than a big change we can't keep up.

288
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:52,120
That doesn't mean big dreams are useless.

289
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,340
Quite the opposite.

290
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,360
You can have big plans.

291
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:59,160
But you don't have to carry all their weight today.

292
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:02,880
You can simply choose the next step.

293
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,640
If you want to read more,

294
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,710
start with a few pages.

295
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,320
If you want to sleep better,

296
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:11,520
try to have a slightly calmer evening.

297
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:13,720
If you want to improve a relationship,

298
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:17,280
maybe start with an honest conversation.

299
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:19,520
And if you want to learn French,

300
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:23,780
listen, speak, read or write a little,

301
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,200
whenever you can.

302
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:28,360
What matters isn't doing it perfectly.

303
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:31,340
It's building a habit that has its place

304
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:32,590
in your real life.

305
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:35,120
Because your real life also includes

306
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:39,960
tiredness, the unexpected, work, responsibilities.

307
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:43,880
And a good change must be able to live in that reality.

308
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:46,760
Not just on an ideal day.

309
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:49,400
I'd also like to talk to you about something else.

310
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:51,830
We sometimes tend to think that if we

311
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:55,120
miss a day, we've lost everything.

312
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,840
But that's not true.

313
00:12:56,840 --> 00:13:00,230
One hard day doesn't destroy all our efforts.

314
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:04,480
A moment of rest doesn't mean we've given up.

315
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,920
You can pick up again.

316
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,880
You can adjust your pace.

317
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:11,120
You can start again without punishing yourself.

318
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,760
And maybe the best question isn't:

319
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,360
"How can I become a completely different person?"

320
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:23,280
But rather: "What small thing can I do differently, right now?"

321
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:26,840
Because a life doesn't always change with one big decision.

322
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:30,300
It can also change with small decisions that

323
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:32,040
become, little by little,

324
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,800
our new way of living.

325
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:38,840
There's something special about the word "tomorrow".

326
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:41,600
Tomorrow, I'll start.

327
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,960
Tomorrow, I'll take care of myself.

328
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:48,560
Tomorrow, I'll be braver.

329
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:51,920
Tomorrow, I'll do things differently.

330
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,080
This word gives us hope.

331
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:57,310
And sometimes, that hope does us good.

332
00:13:57,360 --> 00:14:01,200
But it can also become a way of putting off our life.

333
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:04,960
Imagine someone who keeps a beautiful notebook in a drawer.

334
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:07,090
They bought it to write down their ideas,

335
00:14:07,090 --> 00:14:09,400
their dreams and their thoughts.

336
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:12,880
But every time they want to start, they hesitate.

337
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,880
They want to find the right pen.

338
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,200
They want to have beautiful handwriting.

339
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:21,200
They want to write something important on the first page.

340
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,680
So the notebook stays empty.

341
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:25,040
The days go by.

342
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,470
Then months.

343
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,120
And one evening, they open the drawer,

344
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:32,080
take the notebook and simply write:

345
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:35,920
"Today, I don't really know what to say.

346
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,200
But I'm here."

347
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:39,560
It's not an extraordinary sentence.

348
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:42,640
And yet, something has just changed.

349
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,640
The notebook is no longer a project.

350
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:47,280
It has become part of their life.

351
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:51,880
And maybe our dreams are sometimes like that notebook.

352
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:58,280
We want to start so well that we never start.

353
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,920
We wait to become more organised,

354
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:03,800
smarter, more confident.

355
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:08,050
As if we first had to become a new person

356
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:10,560
to live differently.

357
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,560
But here's the paradox.

358
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:15,840
You don't always become a new person before

359
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:17,960
changing your habits.

360
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:22,300
Sometimes, your new habits help you become the person

361
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:24,060
you want to be.

362
00:15:24,110 --> 00:15:26,280
It goes both ways.

363
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,160
You make a small change.

364
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:31,280
That change gives you a new experience.

365
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:36,960
That experience gently changes the way you see yourself.

366
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,260
And over time,

367
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:41,410
you understand that you're capable of things that

368
00:15:41,410 --> 00:15:45,000
you didn't dare to try before.

369
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:50,120
I find this idea especially important when we look at our past.

370
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:53,230
Maybe you've already given up on some projects.

371
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:56,080
Maybe you've started several times.

372
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:59,880
Maybe you feel like you've wasted time.

373
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:05,520
But your past isn't a final verdict on your future.

374
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:08,860
What you didn't manage yesterday doesn't mean

375
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:12,200
you'll never manage it.

376
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,440
And what you've done for ten years

377
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:19,280
doesn't force you to keep going for the next ten years.

378
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,550
You have the right to learn.

379
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:24,720
You have the right to change your mind.

380
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:29,160
You have the right to choose a different direction.

381
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:32,280
Without denying the person you were before.

382
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:35,210
Because that person was also doing their best with

383
00:16:35,210 --> 00:16:40,680
what they knew, what they felt and what they could do.

384
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:43,840
So, today, I'm not going to ask you to

385
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,320
change your whole life.

386
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:48,630
I'd simply like to ask you a question.

387
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:53,560
What is that small thing you know you could do differently?

388
00:16:53,560 --> 00:16:56,720
Maybe a conversation you keep putting off.

389
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,840
A habit that wears you out.

390
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:02,200
A project you keep in the back of your mind.

391
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:06,320
Or a few minutes you'd like to get back for yourself.

392
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:09,280
You don't need to answer me now.

393
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:12,040
Just take the time to think about it.

394
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:14,000
And if an answer comes up,

395
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:18,460
don't immediately turn it into a huge obligation.

396
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:20,160
Keep it simple.

397
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:24,240
Simple enough to be able to start.

398
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:27,560
Because nothing changes if nothing changes.

399
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:29,970
But as soon as one small thing changes,

400
00:17:29,970 --> 00:17:34,720
even quietly, a new possibility appears.

401
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:38,560
And sometimes, that's all we need

402
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:41,120
to find a direction again.

403
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,480
Before we say goodbye,

404
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:46,030
I'd like you to keep one last thought with you.

405
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:49,240
You don't have to solve everything today.

406
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:51,840
You don't need a perfect plan for

407
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,240
the years ahead.

408
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:56,570
And you don't need to know exactly where

409
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:59,240
each decision will lead you.

410
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:03,480
Life is rarely as clear as we'd like it to be.

411
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:06,560
There are moments when we move forward easily.

412
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:09,760
And others when we need to slow down,

413
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:14,350
to think or simply to rest.

414
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:17,120
All of that is part of the journey.

415
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:20,280
But if something in your life is gently asking

416
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:23,930
to change, maybe you can start listening to it.

417
00:18:23,930 --> 00:18:25,340
No pressure.

418
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:26,880
No comparison.

419
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:30,800
Without asking yourself to become a perfect person.

420
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:34,760
One small step can be enough for today.

421
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,720
And if tomorrow is hard,

422
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,310
you can pick up again when you can.

423
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:44,400
Remember: change isn't a race.

424
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:47,480
It's not a competition with others.

425
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,890
It's a way of getting closer,

426
00:18:49,890 --> 00:18:53,100
little by little, to the life that

427
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,040
means something to you.

428
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,720
Thank you for sharing this moment with me.

429
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:00,610
I hope this conversation brought you a little

430
00:19:00,610 --> 00:19:04,500
calm, a few French words and a new way

431
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:06,760
of looking at your possibilities.

432
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:10,070
And I'd be happy to hear about your experience.

433
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,210
Have you ever had a moment when

434
00:19:12,210 --> 00:19:16,350
a tiny change transformed something important

435
00:19:16,350 --> 00:19:17,200
in your life?

436
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,040
Tell me in the comments.

437
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:21,480
I'd really love to read you.

438
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,920
Take care of yourself.

439
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:26,520
See you very soon on Cozy French Radio.

440
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,520
Bye for now.
